Somebody posted something the other day about having found (and killed, I
think) the Wizard, but not found the Book of the Dead; somebody else suggested
that perhaps the Book had burned. I was thinking about this, and it seems
to me that the Book, as well as the Candelabrum and the Bell are
indestructible, so I think the burning book is out. The other day, I
had the book with me in the Sanctum, stepping on all the fire traps many
times over, and each time the Book glowed red, but didn't burn. I had lost
all my potions, scrolls and other spellbooks to the traps, but the Book
survived. Even in the Fire plane in the endgame I stepped on many fire
traps and the Book never burned. Similarly, I had zapped a wand of cancellation
at the Candelabrum to uncurse it, and this didn't turn it into some
non-magical candlestick. It may be possible to erase the Book by zapping
a wand of cancellation at it, or to polymorph the Book, Candelabrum or Bell
into other spellbooks or tools, but I heven't tried doing this. So as far
as I know these items are pretty much indestructible (and by the way, they
are not needed anymore after entering the Sanctum, so don't bother carrying
them into the endgame). So what could have happened to the Book in this
first post? Is it possible that the Wizard was standing over the moat around
his hideout when he was killed? That would explain it: the Book was lost in
the moat (the first thing the Wizard does when you attack him is pick up
the Book). So be careful! Without the Book, there's no way to finish the
Game. It may be possible to wish for it if it is lost, but I wouldn't count
on it...

